</code></pre> <p>The first returns <code>Ok(())</code> on schema success and <code>Err</code> for violations or execution failures. The report form returns <code>Ok(report)</code> even for schema violations; inspect <code>report.has_errors()</code>. Malformed XML and schema setup failures return <code>Err</code> because validation did not complete.</p> <p><code>ValidationReport</code> contains <code>layers_checked: Vec&lt;ValidationLayer&gt;</code> and <code>issues: Vec&lt;ValidationFinding&gt;</code>. The schema report marks only <code>ValidationLayer::Xsd</code>, including when schema errors were found. An absent layer makes no claim. Convert builder errors using <code>ValidationReport::from(&amp;validation_error)</code> or <code>ValidationFinding::from(&amp;validation_issue)</code>; conversion preserves findings but runs no new checks.</p> <p>Local ZATCA validation</p> <pre><code>validator.validate_zatca(
    xml: &amp;str,
