</code></pre> <p><code>ZatcaValidationOptions</code> has <code>previous_invoice_hash: Option&lt;InvoiceHash&gt;</code> (set it from <code>hash()</code>, <code>hash_xml</code> or <code>text.parse()?</code>) and <code>evaluated_at: Option&lt;chrono::DateTime&lt;chrono::FixedOffset&gt;&gt;</code>. <code>Default::default()</code> omits both. Native callers may omit evaluation time; direct WASM callers must supply it. The 4 KiB JSON limit applies to JSON binding inputs, not this typed options struct.</p> <p><code>ZatcaValidationReport</code> exposes <code>schema_version</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>evaluated_at</code>, and <code>stages</code>. Call <code>is_complete()</code>, <code>has_errors()</code>, and <code>is_valid()</code> for derived outcomes. <code>validation_report()</code> aggregates findings into the shared report; only completed stages contribute checked layers, and both CEN and KSA must complete before <code>BusinessRules</code> is listed. Partial findings remain in the aggregate.</p> <p>On <code>Err(error)</code>, <code>error.report</code> contains the partial <code>Box&lt;ZatcaValidationReport&gt;</code>; <code>error.kind</code>, <code>stage</code>, <code>assertion_site</code>, <code>location</code>, and <code>message</code> describe the failure. Serializing reports includes derived outcomes; deserialization recomputes them from stage coverage. Calls borrow inputs and do not consume invoice objects.</p> <p>Import from <code>fatoora</code>.</p> <pre><code>validate_xml(xml: str) -&gt; bool
validate_zatca(
