</code></pre> <p>The schema function returns <code>True</code> on success; violations raise an exception rather than returning <code>False</code>. <code>validate_zatca</code> returns a frozen <code>ZatcaReport</code> dataclass even when the document is rejected or coverage is incomplete. Inspect <code>report.is_valid</code>, then <code>report.stages</code> (each a <code>ZatcaStageReport</code> with <code>stage</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>findings</code>, <code>evaluated_assertions</code> and <code>provenance</code>) or <code>report.findings</code> for explanations. Each <code>ZatcaFinding</code> has <code>severity</code>, <code>layer</code>, <code>code</code>, <code>message</code>, <code>location</code> and <code>assertion_site</code>. The enums (<code>ZatcaStage</code>, <code>ZatcaStageStatus</code>, <code>Severity</code>, <code>ValidationLayer</code>, <code>ValidationLocationKind</code>) are string enums whose values are the JSON names. <code>report.to_json()</code> returns the JSON report and <code>report.to_dict()</code> the decoded dictionary.</p> <p><code>evaluated_at</code> takes a timezone-aware <code>datetime</code> or RFC 3339 text. Context is encoded as JSON, subject to the 4096-byte options limit; interior NUL characters are rejected. Execution failures raise <code>FatooraError</code>; after validation starts, <code>error.details["report"]</code> contains the partial report as a dictionary. Check whether the key exists because invalid input can fail before a report exists. Validation does not depend on a <code>Config</code>.</p> <p>Import <code>Xml</code> from <code>fatoority</code>.</p> <pre><code>const schemaValid = Xml.validate(xml);
