e normalized native form, so <code>1.50</code> is returned as <code>1.5m</code>; both compare equal. C# <code>decimal</code> and the native decimal share the same 28-digit range.</p> <p>Native object classes implement <code>IDisposable</code>, including returned snapshots. Disposal is idempotent; later calls on that wrapper throw <code>ObjectDisposedException</code>. Finalization provides cleanup if disposal is omitted, but its timing is not deterministic. Releasing an owner does not guarantee zeroization of secrets or copies exported to managed strings and arrays.</p> <p><code>InvoiceBuilder.Build()</code>, <code>InvoiceSigner.Sign()</code>, and <code>SignedInvoice.IntoXml()</code> consume inner state. The outer wrapper remains disposable, but reusing consumed state raises <code>InvalidInputException</code>. Build and signing failures can also consume state. Returned invoice data, totals, addresses, and response children are owned snapshots and remain usable after their parents are disposed.</p> <p>For binary output, dispose the <code>Bytes</code> owner and keep the array returned by <code>ToArray()</code>:</p> <pre><code>using Fatoora;

